(1568099, 209607, 38476, '<td valign="top">I find that dark photos are great if I know what I''m looking at (like a face that''s half in the light, or a building''s silhouette). There''s a dramatic element to it that would be missing if everything was visible. But in this case the darkness is really hindering me: I''m not familiar enough with pilots uniforms to know why the epaulets (if that''s what they are?) are different from each other. Are they from two different uniforms? Is something in front of the one on the right?<br/> <br/>A little more light would really have helped me here...</td>', 'I find that dark photos are great if I know what I''m looking at (like a face that''s half in the light, or a building''s silhouette). There''s a dramatic element to it that would be missing if everything was visible. But in this case the darkness is really hindering me: I''m not familiar enough with pilots uniforms to know why the epaulets (if that''s what they are?) are different from each other. Are they from two different uniforms? Is something in front of the one on the right? A little more light would really have helped me here...', '2005-07-27 19:45:26.000000', NULL, 1),
